<title>USA: Unitrin buys back 227,000 shrs in Q3.</title>
<headline>Unitrin buys back 227,000 shrs in Q3.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unitrin Inc said it repurchased 227,000 of its common shares in open market transactions during the third quarter at an aggregate cost of $10.6 million.</p>
<p>The insurance company has bought back about 14.8 million shares of its common stock at a total cost of $722 million since August 1994.</p>
<p>At the end of the third quarter, it had 37.3 million average shares outstanding, compared to 39.5 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
